From fd16e178e2caaf217b9f1f6abd00494b4a2f115f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher AMIAUD <christopher.amiaud@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:41:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Add job control to threaded fork()

kill(), getppid(), process groups and the terminal's foreground group
now come from the table of processes, so a shell can manage jobs:
kill %1, ^Z then fg or bg, kill 0. A stop signal suspends the thread
of the process until SIGCONT or SIGKILL, wait4() reports stops and
continues, and the parent gets SIGCHLD.

Since a process is signalled without a host signal, blocking pipe
reads and writes, tty reads and nanosleep() look for pending signals
at least every 100ms.

On emscripten the page draws the terminal, so the page reads ^C, ^Z
and ^\ too: blink_tty_isig() tells whether the terminal is in cooked
mode, and blink_tty_signal() sends a signal to the foreground process
group.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
